{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Unusual premium readings"},"description":"Finds unusual premiums, discounts and pricing gaps in the current Bullion Price Check tracked market. For each tracked product: today's lowest and median dealer premium over melt (percent and USD per fine troy ounce) and the pricing gap between them, each compared with the product's own daily history. Lists high_premiums (unusually high premium), discounts (unusually low premium against the product's own history) and pricing_gaps (unusually wide spread between the lowest and median offer). Listed only with at least 30 history days AND |z| >= 3, where z uses a spread floor of 0.25 pp and is shown capped at 5, AND at least minimum_deviation_pp from the history median; with fewer days nothing is listed. Products are held back (held_back, with reasons, never listed) when, at any dealer price used, spot moved at least spot_move_hold_pct (default 0.5%) since that price's time (spot_moved) or that move cannot be checked (spot_move_unknown), because dealer prices lag spot; when the usually cheapest dealer has no fresh price today or fewer than 80% of the usual dealers do; or when the stored history is old. period_days 1: day-over-day against yesterday's daily median, low-confidence, in day_over_day_changes only. Uses only in-stock bank (check/ACH/wire) offers within the 120-minute price freshness limit and a spot price within its 120-minute limit. A description of the market, not advice; no dealer names. Standard tool free; for a version fine-tuned or customized to your business, email for pricing via https://bullionpricecheck.com/contact/.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"examples":[{"metal":"all","period_days":30},{"metal":"silver","minimum_deviation_pp":1,"period_days":7},{"metal":"gold","period_days":1},{"metal":"gold","period_days":30,"spot_move_hold_pct":1}],"properties":{"metal":{"default":"all","descr